        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor: remove dead plugin loader exports",
        "body": "Related: #105595\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe enforced unused-export ratchet still carried roughly 570 `src/plugins/` entries, leaving a large amount of dead internal surface and weakening the baseline as an actionable cleanup signal.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nRemove unused plugin-loader exports in coherent ownership groups, keeping implementations local when still used internally and deleting tests that only covered deleted code. Preserve plugin SDK barrels, manifest contracts, dynamic loader/report entry points, and other shipped surfaces; keep the few remaining test-only controls in Knip-ignored core test fixtures.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior change. Maintainers get a substantially smaller dead-export baseline and less accidental internal API surface around plugin loading.\n\nThis PR is AI-assisted; the resulting code and contracts were reviewed and validated.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Production Knip baseline: `src/plugins/` entries reduced from 574 to 7 intentional shipped/dynamic contracts; the current-main-integrated baseline matches 4,334 entries.\n- Final `pnpm deadcode:exports:update` was byte-stable at SHA-256 `792d3def5fda53e4962604b4e3309a6212dad25f76ee15faa51500caefac571f`; `pnpm deadcode:exports` passed on Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxd5bw76r3pg69gz5f3ef1es`.\n- `pnpm check:changed` passed all selected format, SDK, type, lint, policy, cycle, database, and Docker scheduler lanes in 13m52s on an earlier exact integrated head.\n- Focused catalog/envelope/index tests: 55/55 passed. The exact-pinned npm integrity-drift regression remains covered through the supported update entry point with a test-local callback fixture; `src/plugins/update.test.ts` passes 116/116, targeted format passes, and targeted lint reports zero warnings and errors.\n- Isolated real lifecycle proof on the same Testbox: pinned npm install of `@openclaw/irc@2026.6.11`; `plugins inspect irc --runtime --json` reported `activated: true`, `status: loaded`, and the IRC channel capability; update reported the pinned version current; a second runtime inspection remained loaded; uninstall removed the config entry, install record, and installed directory, then inspection confirmed only the bundled disabled fallback with no install record.\n- On the final corrected-main head, `pnpm tsgo:core`, `pnpm tsgo:ui`, `pnpm tsgo:extensions`, the complete `pnpm tsgo:test` sequence, and `pnpm plugin-sdk:surface:check` passed on the same Testbox. `pnpm build` passed on the preceding exact integrated head.\n- Structured autoreview covered the large refactor in coherent chunks; accepted invariant/security findings were fixed. The restored integrity regression received a fresh clean review with 0.96 confidence and no actionable findings.\n",
